{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790288437,"nonce":"+0iT1rQKaI6yNRGMpxFLio68B4g=","title":"macOS: a trace in hybrid mode misses compiled frames, so the whole unit suite fails testExceptionStack","message":"8f23bd5 fixed this on Linux: interpreted and compiled frames merge by\nstack address, which needs every compiled frame reported with its CFA. On\nmacOS (aarch64) the unwinder reports none. `ASH_TRACE_WALK=1 ash --mode\nhybrid bin/unit.hl` over the whole unit suite (debug build, 2026-09-24):\n9386 `[trace-walk] runtime` lines, 0 `compiled`, 0 `unknown`, 0 `chain`.\nThe walk ends at the first JIT frame, which has no unwind entry the\nunwinder can use, and unlike x86-64 Linux there is no frame-pointer\ncontinuation from it. With `compiled` empty, `trace_sites` takes the\nunaddressed order, and the frames reached through the stub bridge land in\nthe wrong place.\n\nSymptom: `ash --mode hybrid --quiet bin/unit.hl` (4.3.6 suite) fails\ntestExceptionStack deterministically on the Mac (`checkSetup expected, but\ngot runSetup/then/runTest`); the same case isolated passes, interp passes,\nand the NUC's Linux build passes whole-suite hybrid. Also fails on 7f11e13,\nso it predates 2026-09-24's commits; not tied to OSR (`ASH_OSR=0`) or the\ncollector (`ASH_GC_GEN=0`).\n\nLikely fix: continue the walk from the stopping frame by frame pointers, as\nx86-64 Linux does (aarch64 compiled code keeps x29, and the runtime does on\nmacOS), or register the JIT's unwind info with the macOS unwinder.","files":null}]}